IMPORT prelude

-- Patents Act 1990 (Cth) -- the questions of the inventor and founder.
--
-- SEAT: the inventor or founder who wants to patent an invention, alone or through the company (in the WA lives, Daniel for
-- Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd and its matching engine): "Is my invention (my software) a patentable invention?",
-- "Should I seek a standard patent or an innovation patent?", "How long will my patent last?", "Who may be granted the
-- patent: me, or the company?", "Does my own earlier disclosure count against me?".
--
-- Provisions covered: novelty, inventive step and innovative step as the Act frames them (s 7(1)-(4)); usefulness (s 7A);
-- secret use (s 9); exclusive rights during the term (s 13(1)); who may be granted a patent (s 15); co-ownership (s 16(1));
-- patentable inventions for a standard and an innovation patent (s 18); validity and entitlement (s 22A); publication or use
-- on or after the priority date (s 23); information disregarded -- the grace period (s 24); priority dates (s 43(2)); the
-- innovation patent formalities bar (s 52(3)); date of patent (s 65); term (ss 67, 68); revocation for want of entitlement
-- (s 138(3)(a), (4)); ceasing for unpaid renewal fees (s 143).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 52, compilation date 14 October 2024 (includes amendments up to Act No. 39, 2024), register id
-- C2024C00455, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04014.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). The deposit's own
-- caveat: a version in force from 19 September 2026 has no registered compilation yet, so later amendments may be missing.
-- The Patents Regulations 1991 are NOT deposited: the "prescribed circumstances" and "prescribed period" of s 24(1), the
-- "prescribed period" of s 9(e), the regulation dates of ss 43(2)(a) and 65(b), and renewal fees and periods (s 143) are
-- INPUTS. The amending Act No. 9, 2020 is NOT deposited; the day s 52(3) commenced is taken from the endnotes (see s 52).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the prior art base and prior art information as defined in Schedule 1 (the novelty and step judgments are
-- inputs); manner of manufacture (s 18(1)(a) points to s 6 of the Statute of Monopolies and the cases -- an input); the
-- application, examination, opposition and grant procedure (Chs 3-6, 9A); PCT and Convention applications (ss 29A, 29B);
-- specifications (s 40); amendments (Ch 10); extension of term for pharmaceutical substances (ss 70-79A); infringement and
-- exemptions (Ch 11); compulsory licences and Crown use (Chs 12, 17); revocation on grounds other than entitlement; patent
-- attorneys, the Commissioner and courts (machinery or not met by the seat); fees.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. 0 means "no such date".
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the inventor or founder, with the design
-- defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use
-- as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Patents Act 1990 -- the inventor and founder`

§§ `dates -- periods in months and years`

-- The Act does not define how a period of months or years is counted. INFERENCE: a period of N months from a date ends on
-- the same-numbered day N months later, or on the last day of that month if it has no such day (the rule the Trade Marks Act
-- 1995 s 6A states and the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 is usually read to give). So 20 years from 29 February 2032 ends on
-- 28 February 2052.

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a leap year` MEANS
        (`y` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (`y` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  `y` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
      `m` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in month` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `m` EQUALS 2 THEN IF `is a leap year` `y` THEN 29 ELSE 28
           IF `m` EQUALS 4 OR `m` EQUALS 6 OR `m` EQUALS 9 OR `m` EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

@export On what day does a period of so many months from this date end?
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date the period runs from, written YYYYMMDD
      `months` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of months in the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day a period of months ends` IS
    `new year` TIMES 10000 PLUS `new month` TIMES 100 PLUS `new day`
    WHERE
        `y` MEANS TRUNC (`the date` / 10000) 0
        `m` MEANS TRUNC ((`the date` MODULO 10000) / 100) 0
        `d` MEANS `the date` MODULO 100
        `count` MEANS `y` TIMES 12 PLUS (`m` MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        `new year` MEANS TRUNC (`count` / 12) 0
        `new month` MEANS (`count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `new day` MEANS IF `d` GREATER THAN `days in month` `new year` `new month`
                        THEN `days in month` `new year` `new month`
                        ELSE `d`

§§ `the facts I can state`

-- PatentKind: a standard patent or an innovation patent (Schedule 1: "patent means a standard patent or an innovation
-- patent").
DECLARE PatentKind IS ONE OF
    `a standard patent`
    `an innovation patent`

-- Application: my application and its dates, as I would state them.
--   `date of filing of my complete specification` -- s 65(a): ordinarily the date of the patent.
--   `date the regulations fix as the date of the patent` -- s 65(b): 0 if the regulations fix none (regulations not
--     deposited; an input).
--   `date of filing of the specification containing my claim` -- s 43(2)(b): ordinarily the priority date of the claim.
--   `date the regulations fix as the priority date of my claim` -- s 43(2)(a), (2A): for example where an earlier
--     (provisional or Convention) document discloses the invention; 0 if s 43(2A) does not apply (an input).
--   `months in the prescribed period for my own disclosure` -- s 24(1): the "prescribed period" within which the complete
--     application must be made (regulations not deposited; an input).
--   `it meets the other formalities requirements` -- s 52 Note 3: the other requirements are in the regulations (an input).
DECLARE Application HAS
    `the kind of patent I apply for` IS A PatentKind
    `date of filing of my complete specification` IS A NUMBER
    `date the regulations fix as the date of the patent` IS A NUMBER
    `date of filing of the specification containing my claim` IS A NUMBER
    `date the regulations fix as the priority date of my claim` IS A NUMBER
    `months in the prescribed period for my own disclosure` IS A NUMBER
    `it meets the other formalities requirements` IS A BOOLEAN

-- PriorUse: how my invention was used in Australia, by me or with my authority (or by my predecessor in title), before the
-- priority date, without being made public (s 9, s 18(1)(d)). "Secret use" is not defined beyond s 9; whether a use was
-- secret is asked as a fact.
DECLARE PriorUse IS ONE OF
    `no secret use`
    `for reasonable trial or experiment only`
    `solely in the course of a confidential disclosure`
    `for a purpose other than trade or commerce`
    `by a government I had disclosed it to`
    `for trade, with a complete application within the prescribed period`
    `for trade, with no complete application within the prescribed period`

-- Invention: the invention as claimed, and the judgments the Act hands to the Commissioner or a court, as inputs.
--   The novelty, inventive-step and innovative-step judgments (s 7) are asked LEAVING ASIDE my own earlier disclosure, and
--   then whether that disclosure, if it counted, would defeat them; s 24 decides whether it counts.
--   "manner of manufacture" (s 18(1)(a)) is "within the meaning of section 6 of the Statute of Monopolies": the Act says no
--   more, so whether software is one is for the cases -- an input, "if the Commissioner or court is satisfied".
DECLARE Invention HAS
    `it is a manner of manufacture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is novel, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it involves an inventive step, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it involves an innovative step, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my own earlier disclosure, if counted, would defeat its novelty or step` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the complete specification discloses a specific, substantial and credible use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that disclosure is enough for a skilled person to appreciate that use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is otherwise useful` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a human being or a biological process for generating one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a plant or animal or a biological process for generating one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a microbiological process or a product of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how it was used before the priority date` IS A PriorUse

-- DisclosureKind: how my invention was made public before I applied (s 24).
DECLARE DisclosureKind IS ONE OF
    `no earlier disclosure`
    `by me or with my consent, in the prescribed circumstances`
    `by me or with my consent, in other circumstances`
    `by someone who got it from me, without my consent`
    `only to a government, or a person it authorised to investigate the invention`

DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `how my invention was made public` IS A DisclosureKind
    `the day it was made public` IS A NUMBER

§§ `s 43 -- priority date`

-- s 43(2): "The priority date of a claim is: (a) if subsection (2A) applies to the claim--the date determined under the
-- regulations; or (b) otherwise--the date of the filing of the specification."
@export What is the priority date of my claim (s 43(2))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the priority date of my claim` IS
    IF `my application`'s `date the regulations fix as the priority date of my claim` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `my application`'s `date the regulations fix as the priority date of my claim`
    ELSE `my application`'s `date of filing of the specification containing my claim`

§§ `ss 23, 24 -- my own earlier disclosure (the grace period)`

-- s 23: "A patent is not invalid ... merely because of: (a) the publication or use of the invention ... on or after the
-- priority date of that claim".
-- s 24(1): "For the purpose of deciding whether an invention is novel or involves an inventive step or an innovative step,
-- the person making the decision must disregard: (a) any information made publicly available in the prescribed
-- circumstances, by or with the consent of the nominated person or patentee ...; and (b) any information made publicly
-- available without the consent of the nominated person or patentee, through any publication or use of the invention by
-- another person who derived the information from the nominated person or patentee ...; but only if a complete application
-- for the invention is made within the prescribed period."
-- s 24(2): information given "to any of the following, but to no other person or organisation: (i) the Commonwealth or a
-- State or Territory, or an authority ...; (ii) a person authorised by the Commonwealth or a State or Territory to
-- investigate the invention" must also be disregarded, with no time limit.
-- INFERENCE: the prescribed period is counted from the day the information was made public (the regulations, which say,
-- are not deposited). The complete application is taken to be made on the date its complete specification is filed.

@export Did I make my complete application within the prescribed period after my disclosure (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I apply within the grace period` IF
    `my application`'s `date of filing of my complete specification`
        AT MOST `the day a period of months ends` (`my disclosure`'s `the day it was made public`)
                                                  (`my application`'s `months in the prescribed period for my own disclosure`)

@export Must my own earlier disclosure be disregarded in judging novelty and the inventive or innovative step (s 24)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my disclosure be disregarded` IF
    CONSIDER `my disclosure`'s `how my invention was made public`
    WHEN `no earlier disclosure` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `by me or with my consent, in the prescribed circumstances` THEN `Did I apply within the grace period` `my application` `my disclosure`
    WHEN `by someone who got it from me, without my consent` THEN `Did I apply within the grace period` `my application` `my disclosure`
    WHEN `only to a government, or a person it authorised to investigate the invention` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by me or with my consent, in other circumstances` THEN FALSE

@export Does my own earlier disclosure count against my invention (ss 23, 24)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my disclosure count against me` IF
        (NOT (`my disclosure`'s `how my invention was made public` EQUALS `no earlier disclosure`))
    AND `my disclosure`'s `the day it was made public` LESS THAN `What is the priority date of my claim` `my application`
    AND (NOT (`Must my disclosure be disregarded` `my application` `my disclosure`))

§§ `ss 7, 7A, 9 -- novel, a step, useful, not secretly used`

-- s 7(1): an invention "is to be taken to be novel when compared with the prior art base unless it is not novel in the light
-- of" prior art information. s 7(2): it "is to be taken to involve an inventive step ... unless the invention would have been
-- obvious to a person skilled in the relevant art in the light of the common general knowledge". s 7(4): it "is to be taken to
-- involve an innovative step ... unless [it] would ... only vary from the kinds of information ... in ways that make no
-- substantial contribution to the working of the invention". These are the Commissioner's or court's judgments: inputs.

GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application
      `the invention` IS AN Invention
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my disclosure defeats it` MEANS
        `Does my disclosure count against me` `my application` `my disclosure`
    AND `the invention`'s `my own earlier disclosure, if counted, would defeat its novelty or step`

@export Is my invention novel (ss 7(1), 18(1)(b)(i), 24)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my invention novel` IF
        `the invention`'s `it is novel, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure`
    AND (NOT (`my disclosure defeats it` `my application` `the invention` `my disclosure`))

@export Does my invention involve the step my kind of patent needs -- inventive for a standard patent, innovative for an innovation patent (ss 7(2), (4), 18(1)(b)(ii), (1A)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my invention involve the required step` IF
        `the step aside from my disclosure`
    AND (NOT (`my disclosure defeats it` `my application` `the invention` `my disclosure`))
    WHERE
        `the step aside from my disclosure` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my application`'s `the kind of patent I apply for`
            WHEN `a standard patent` THEN `the invention`'s `it involves an inventive step, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure`
            WHEN `an innovation patent` THEN `the invention`'s `it involves an innovative step, leaving aside my own earlier disclosure`

-- s 7A(1): "an invention is taken not to be useful unless a specific, substantial and credible use for the invention (so far
-- as claimed) is disclosed in the complete specification." (2): the disclosure "must be sufficient for that specific,
-- substantial and credible use to be appreciated by a person skilled in the relevant art." (3): s 7A "does not otherwise
-- affect the meaning of the word useful".
@export Is my invention useful (ss 7A, 18(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my invention useful` IF
        `the invention`'s `the complete specification discloses a specific, substantial and credible use`
    AND `the invention`'s `that disclosure is enough for a skilled person to appreciate that use`
    AND `the invention`'s `it is otherwise useful`

-- s 18(1)(d): the invention must not have been "secretly used in the patent area before the priority date of that claim by,
-- or on behalf of, or with the authority of, the patentee or nominated person or [their] predecessor in title".
-- s 9: not secret use -- (a) "reasonable trial or experiment only"; (b) "solely in the course of a confidential disclosure";
-- (c) "any other use ... for any purpose other than the purpose of trade or commerce"; (d) use by a government to which the
-- invention was disclosed; (e) use "for any purpose, if a complete application is made for the invention within the
-- prescribed period".
@export Was my invention secretly used before the priority date in a way that defeats it (ss 9, 18(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my invention secretly used` IF
    `the invention`'s `how it was used before the priority date` EQUALS `for trade, with no complete application within the prescribed period`

§§ `s 18 -- patentable inventions`

-- s 18(1): "an invention is a patentable invention for the purposes of a standard patent if the invention, so far as claimed
-- in any claim: (a) is a manner of manufacture within the meaning of section 6 of the Statute of Monopolies; and (b) when
-- compared with the prior art base as it existed before the priority date of that claim: (i) is novel; and (ii) involves an
-- inventive step; and (c) is useful; and (d) was not secretly used". s 18(1A): the same for an innovation patent, with "(ii)
-- involves an innovative step".
-- s 18(2): "Human beings, and the biological processes for their generation, are not patentable inventions."
-- s 18(3): "For the purposes of an innovation patent, plants and animals, and the biological processes for the generation of
-- plants and animals, are not patentable inventions." (4): "Subsection (3) does not apply if the invention is a
-- microbiological process or a product of such a process."

-- Patentability: the answer, with the first limb that fails, in the order of s 18.
DECLARE Patentability IS ONE OF
    `patentable`
    `not patentable: human beings and their generation (s 18(2))`
    `not patentable for an innovation patent: plants and animals (s 18(3))`
    `not patentable: not a manner of manufacture (s 18(1)(a))`
    `not patentable: not novel (s 18(1)(b)(i))`
    `not patentable: no inventive step (s 18(1)(b)(ii))`
    `not patentable: no innovative step (s 18(1A)(b)(ii))`
    `not patentable: not useful (s 18(1)(c))`
    `not patentable: secretly used before the priority date (s 18(1)(d))`

@export Is my invention a patentable invention, and if not, why not (s 18)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A Patentability
DECIDE `Is my invention patentable` IS
    BRANCH IF `the invention`'s `it is a human being or a biological process for generating one`
              THEN `not patentable: human beings and their generation (s 18(2))`
           IF     `my application`'s `the kind of patent I apply for` EQUALS `an innovation patent`
              AND `the invention`'s `it is a plant or animal or a biological process for generating one`
              AND (NOT (`the invention`'s `it is a microbiological process or a product of one`))
              THEN `not patentable for an innovation patent: plants and animals (s 18(3))`
           IF (NOT (`the invention`'s `it is a manner of manufacture`))
              THEN `not patentable: not a manner of manufacture (s 18(1)(a))`
           IF (NOT (`Is my invention novel` `my application` `the invention` `my disclosure`))
              THEN `not patentable: not novel (s 18(1)(b)(i))`
           IF (NOT (`Does my invention involve the required step` `my application` `the invention` `my disclosure`))
              THEN IF `my application`'s `the kind of patent I apply for` EQUALS `a standard patent`
                   THEN `not patentable: no inventive step (s 18(1)(b)(ii))`
                   ELSE `not patentable: no innovative step (s 18(1A)(b)(ii))`
           IF (NOT (`Is my invention useful` `the invention`))
              THEN `not patentable: not useful (s 18(1)(c))`
           IF `Was my invention secretly used` `the invention`
              THEN `not patentable: secretly used before the priority date (s 18(1)(d))`
           OTHERWISE `patentable`

@export Is my invention a patentable invention (s 18)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `the invention` IS AN Invention @desc Your invention as claimed, and the judgments made of it
      `my disclosure` IS A Disclosure @desc How and when your invention was made public before you applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I seeking a patent for a patentable invention` IF
    `Is my invention patentable` `my application` `the invention` `my disclosure` EQUALS `patentable`

§§ `ss 52(3), 65, 67, 68 -- standard or innovation patent; date and term`

-- s 65: "The date of a patent is: (a) the date of filing of the relevant complete specification; or (b) where the
-- regulations provide for the determination of a different date as the date of a patent--the date determined under the
-- regulations."
@export What is the date of my patent (s 65)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the date of my patent` IS
    IF `my application`'s `date the regulations fix as the date of the patent` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `my application`'s `date the regulations fix as the date of the patent`
    ELSE `my application`'s `date of filing of my complete specification`

-- s 52(3): "It is a requirement of the formalities check that the date of the patent (if granted) would be a date before the
-- day this subsection commences." Note 1: "This subsection was inserted by the Intellectual Property Laws Amendment
-- (Productivity Commission Response Part 2 and Other Measures) Act 2020."
-- The Act's text does not state that day. Endnote 3 of the deposit gives the commencement of Act No. 9, 2020 as "Sch 1
-- (items 2-9): 26 Aug 2021" (the other Schedules commencing on 27 Feb 2020 or 26 Aug 2020). INFERENCE, not read in the
-- deposit: s 52(3) is among Sch 1 items 2-9 and so commenced on 26 August 2021. The amending Act is not deposited.
@export On what day did s 52(3) commence, closing the innovation patent to patents dated from then on (endnote 3; an inference)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day s 52(3) commenced` IS 20210826

@export Can my application for an innovation patent pass the formalities check (s 52(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my innovation patent application pass the formalities check` IF
        `What is the date of my patent` `my application` LESS THAN `the day s 52(3) commenced`
    AND `my application`'s `it meets the other formalities requirements`

-- s 67: "The term of a standard patent is 20 years from the date of the patent."
-- s 68: "The term of an innovation patent is 8 years from the date of the patent."
@export How many years is the term of my patent (ss 67, 68)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A PatentKind @desc A standard patent or an innovation patent
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years is the term of my patent` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a standard patent` THEN 20
    WHEN `an innovation patent` THEN 8

@export On what day does the term of my patent end (ss 65, 67, 68)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `When does the term of my patent end` IS
    `the day a period of months ends` (`What is the date of my patent` `my application`)
                                      (12 TIMES `How many years is the term of my patent` (`my application`'s `the kind of patent I apply for`))

-- s 13(1): "a patent gives the patentee the exclusive rights, during the term of the patent, to exploit the invention and to
-- authorise another person to exploit the invention."
-- s 143: "A standard patent ceases if the patentee: (a) does not pay a renewal fee for the patent within the prescribed
-- period; or (b) does not file the prescribed documents (if any) within the prescribed period." The fees and periods are in
-- the regulations (not deposited): whether I missed one is an input.
-- INFERENCE: the rights are held from grant; the term itself runs from the date of the patent, which is earlier.
@export Do I hold the exclusive rights on this day (ss 13(1), 67, 68, 143)?
GIVEN `my application` IS AN Application @desc Your application and its dates
      `the patent has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the patent been granted to you?
      `I missed a renewal fee or prescribed document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to pay a renewal fee, or file a prescribed document, within the prescribed period?
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you are asking about, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I hold the exclusive rights on this day` IF
        `the patent has been granted`
    AND (NOT `I missed a renewal fee or prescribed document`)
    AND `the day` AT LEAST `What is the date of my patent` `my application`
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `When does the term of my patent end` `my application`

§§ `ss 15, 16, 22A, 138 -- who may be granted the patent`

-- s 15(1): "a patent for an invention may only be granted to a person who: (a) is the inventor; or (b) would, on the grant of
-- a patent for the invention, be entitled to have the patent assigned to the person; or (c) derives title to the invention
-- from the inventor or a person mentioned in paragraph (b); or (d) is the legal representative of a deceased person mentioned
-- in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)." s 15(2): "whether or not he or she is an Australian citizen."
-- The Act says nothing more about an employee's invention. Whether my employer "would ... be entitled to have the patent
-- assigned" turns on the contract of employment and the general law -- a borrowed question, asked as a fact.

-- Claimant: a person (me, or my company) asking whether the patent may be granted to them.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `I am the inventor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on grant I would be entitled to have the patent assigned to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I derive title to the invention from the inventor or such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the legal representative of such a person who has died` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May the patent be granted to me (s 15)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Claimant @desc Who you are in relation to the invention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the patent be granted to me` IF
       `me`'s `I am the inventor`
    OR `me`'s `on grant I would be entitled to have the patent assigned to me`
    OR `me`'s `I derive title to the invention from the inventor or such a person`
    OR `me`'s `I am the legal representative of such a person who has died`

-- s 22A: "A patent is not invalid merely because: (a) the patent, or a share in the patent, was granted to a person who was not
-- entitled to it; or (b) ... was not granted to a person who was entitled to it."
-- s 138(3)(a): a court may revoke a patent on the ground "that the patentee is not entitled to the patent"; (4): "A court must
-- not make an order ... on the ground that the patentee is not entitled to the patent unless the court is satisfied that, in
-- all the circumstances, it is just and equitable to do so."
@export Can my patent be revoked because I was not entitled to it (ss 22A, 138(3)(a), (4))?
GIVEN `I was not entitled to the patent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the patent granted to you when you were not entitled to it?
      `the court is satisfied revocation is just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied it is just and equitable, in all the circumstances, to revoke it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my patent be revoked for want of entitlement` IF
    `I was not entitled to the patent` AND `the court is satisfied revocation is just and equitable`

-- s 16(1): "Subject to any agreement to the contrary, where there are 2 or more patentees: (a) each of them is entitled to an
-- equal undivided share in the patent; (b) each of them is entitled to exercise the exclusive rights ... for his or her own
-- benefit without accounting to the others; and (c) none of them can grant a licence under the patent, or assign an interest
-- in it, without the consent of the others."
@export What share of the patent do I hold as one of several patentees (s 16(1)(a))?
GIVEN `number of patentees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many patentees there are, you included
      `the share our agreement gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc The share an agreement between you gives you, as a fraction; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of the patent do I hold` IS
    IF `the share our agreement gives me` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the share our agreement gives me`
    ELSE 1 / `number of patentees`

@export May I grant a licence or assign an interest without the other patentees' consent (s 16(1)(c))?
GIVEN `number of patentees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many patentees there are, you included
      `our agreement lets me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement between you let you do so without the others' consent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I license or assign without the others` IF
    `number of patentees` EQUALS 1 OR `our agreement lets me`
